"[[quarkus-tls-registry_quarkus-tls-ssl-engine]] [.property-path]##link:#quarkus-tls-registry_quarkus-tls-ssl-engine[`+++quarkus.tls.ssl-engine+++`]##\n"
"config_property_copy_button:+++quarkus.tls.ssl-engine+++[]\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"[.description]\n"
"--\n"
"Forces the SSL engine to use.\n"
"\n"
"When not set, Vert.x selects the engine automatically: if `pqc-enforcement-policy` is `strict` or `client-negotiated`, it prefers the JDK engine (JDK 27{plus}) or falls back to OpenSSL. For `relaxed` policy it uses the JDK engine by default.\n"
"\n"
"Use `OPENSSL` to force netty-tcnative (requires the native library on the classpath). Use `JDKSSL` to force the standard JDK SSL engine.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:+++QUARKUS_TLS_SSL_ENGINE+++[]\n"
"--"
msgstr ""

